2:["$","div",null,{"children":["$","div",null,{"className":"article_main__fHCmv","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"article_container__ruma5","children":[["$","$L7",null,{"href":"/blog/an-anthology","className":"article_breadcrumb__DNfec","children":"An Anthology of Joy and Thought Vol. 1"}],["$","$L9",null,{"className":"article_image__M_D4j","src":"/blog/an-anthology/12.jpg","width":600,"height":600,"alt":"article image"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"article_credit__mM_9T","children":"Image: Stephen Noh"}],["$","h1",null,{"className":"article_title__VBWZq","children":"sunshine and rainbows"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"article_text__PI1tP","children":["Sunshine and rainbows. Words that are often used to describe life. To me, they mean light and promise. Light that exposes all darkness and a promise that is unchanging and stretches across all skies.",["$","br",null,{}],["$","br",null,{}],"Then the storms come. They bring about gray skies, darkness. The light we once saw feels distant and the promise unkept.",["$","br",null,{}],["$","br",null,{}],"But then the water falls. Scattered and tattered it covers the earth. Wasn’t water supposed to bring life? For gentle drops nourish but floods consume. How will I choose to view this water?",["$","br",null,{}],["$","br",null,{}],"Consume or nourish, only time and peace will tell. Eventually the storm passes. Has it nourished or consumed, I do not know. But then the light comes out again, and the rainbow forms. The light and the promises I am reminded.",["$","br",null,{}],["$","br",null,{}],"And I remember…",["$","br",null,{}],["$","br",null,{}],"I am home…"]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"article_buttons__s4Lvk","children":[["$","$L7",null,{"href":"/blog/an-anthology/11","className":"article_href__ebsac","children":"<  Previous"}],["$","$L7",null,{"href":"/blog/an-anthology/13","className":"article_href__ebsac","children":"Next  >"}]]}]]}]}]
8:[["$","meta","0",{"name":"viewport","content":"width=device-width, initial-scale=1"}],["$","meta","1",{"charSet":"utf-8"}],["$","title","2",{"children":"Agora | Georgia Tech’s Christian Thought Journal"}],["$","meta","3",{"name":"description","content":"Agora seeks to glorify God as an ecumenical forum and journal of Christian thought. By creating and curating pieces that reflect the vibrant beauty of God’s nature, we offer a collective Christian perspective to the campus dialogue."}],["$","link","4",{"rel":"icon","href":"/logo-black.png","media":"(prefers-color-scheme: light)"}],["$","link","5",{"rel":"icon","href":"/logo-white.png","media":"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)"}],["$","meta","6",{"name":"next-size-adjust"}]]
